---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About Where to Apply · Tech job board aggregator" description="Why Where to Apply exists and how its tech job directory is maintained.">
  <main class="wrap py-16 md:py-24">
    <a class="link text-sm" href="/">← Where to Apply</a>
    <h1 class="mt-8 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">About Where to Apply</h1>
    <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
      <p>Where to Apply is a free directory for people looking for software, AI engineer, and forward deployed engineer (FDE) jobs in India or remote. Job seekers often have to search many company career pages, startup boards, venture capital portfolio sites, communities, and social accounts to discover opportunities. This project brings useful starting points together so a search can begin in one place.</p>
      <p>The directory includes job boards, startup and company career pages, remote platforms, AI and FDE resources, hiring managers and communities, plus a search builder for common hiring platforms. Category and city pages offer focused views. Each entry includes a short note about why it may be useful. The list is a discovery resource, not a guarantee that a role is currently open or that an employer will respond.</p>
      <p>Where to Apply is built and maintained by Hardikk Kamboj as a public project. Source links are reviewed periodically, and contributions that add useful sources or correct outdated information are welcome through the project repository. There is no sign-up and no affiliate link program. Applications happen on the destination sites, whose terms and privacy practices apply there.</p>
      <p>Browse the <a class="link" href="/">directory</a>, read the <a class="link" href="/llms.txt">agent instructions</a>, or <a class="link" href="/contact">get in touch</a> with a correction or question.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
